From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbtp: raise fan TACH upper non-critical threshold to 9500 RPM

MB_FAN0/1_TACH upper non-critical was 8500 RPM, but the fans legitimately run
8500-9000 RPM in normal operation and ramp to ~9200 RPM (failsafe) when the
host is off and PECI/DTS drops out.  That sits inside the normal range, so the
"Upper Non-critical going high" event asserted/deasserted constantly, flapping
the SEL.

Raise the upper non-critical to 9500 RPM - above the observed failsafe maximum
(9212 RPM) so normal/failsafe operation is quiet, while still warning if a fan
genuinely overspeeds.  Upper critical (11500 RPM) is left unchanged as the hard
overspeed alarm.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform configuration]
---
 configurations/fbtp.json | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/configurations/fbtp.json
+++ b/configurations/fbtp.json
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@
           "Direction": "greater than",
           "Name": "upper non critical",
           "Severity": 0,
-          "Value": 8500
+          "Value": 9500
         },
         {
           "Direction": "greater than",
@@ -220,7 +220,7 @@
           "Direction": "greater than",
           "Name": "upper non critical",
           "Severity": 0,
-          "Value": 8500
+          "Value": 9500
         },
